KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 12 --unwind 10 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ virtual base constructed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Meaningful only with the MSVC STL (Windows); elsewhere the #error makes it
fail.  On VS 2022 (CI run for d5afeb79ad) assertion 1 fails: the
istringstream constructed from a string and an allocator does not have
precision() 6.  Not reproduced locally (no MSVC headers).
